Short description
-----------------

xfem1

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM (XFEM) approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree subdivision for integration.

 NOTE: the following problems are similar to this problem but use a different 
 technique:

 body_fitted1:

   Boundary (body) fitted mesh. The mesh is made by invoking
   mesh_cylinder_in_box1 < meshinput1.txt

 fic_dom1:

   Fictitious domain technique.
 
 Use gnu1.gpi to compare the pressure and vorticity on the cylinder for the 
 three different methods.

xfem2

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.

 This problem is similar to xfem1, but now with a better integration technique.

xfem3

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Fluid described by a layer.
 Plot a layer.

 This problem is similar to xfem2, but now the fluid is defined by a layer.

xfem4

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylindrical shaped drop.
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder for
 a coupling of velocities on the interface between the two fluids.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Fluids described by layers.
 Plot a layer.

xfem5

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.

 This problem is similar to xfem2, with the following changes:
   * use of parameter split_threshold to avoid "holes" in interfaces
   * prebuild of all the eltrees in elements near the interface

xfem6

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Fluid described by a layer.
 Plot a layer.

 This problem is similar to xfem3, with the following changes:
   * use of parameter split_threshold to avoid "holes" in interfaces
   * prebuild of all the eltrees in elements near the interface

xfem7

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylindrical shaped drop.
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder for
 a coupling of velocities on the interface between the two fluids.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Fluids described by layers.
 Plot a layer.

 This problem is similar to xfem4, with the following changes:
   * use of parameter split_threshold to avoid "holes" in interfaces
   * prebuild of all the eltrees in elements near the interface

xfem8

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.

 This problem is similar to xfem5, with the following changes:
   * Removal of elements from eltree if integration area is too small.
   * High-order exact integration for small integration areas.
   * embedded Dirichlet boundary condition (eDbc)
   * use of elementset to build the eDbc.
   * optional non-zero imposed velocity of the cylinder.

xfem9

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.

 This problem is similar to xfem8, with the following changes:
   * symmetric embedded Dirichlet boundary condition
   * optional: Nitsche's method.

xfem10

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.

 This problem is similar to xfem8, with the following changes:
   * Baumann-Oden embedded Dirichlet boundary condition

xfem11

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylinder
 eXtended FEM approach with weak constraint on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.

 This problem is similar to xfem2, with the following changes:
   * generalized Newtonian fluid ( Carreau viscosity model)

xfem12

 3D Stokes problem on a cubic domain with a sphere
 eXtended FEM approach with embedded Dirichlet condition on the sphere.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Prebuild eltree for all elements crossing the interface.
 Removal of elements from eltree if integration area is too small.
 High-order exact integration for small integration volumes.
 Optional non-zero imposed velocity of the sphere.
 Optional symmetric matrix.
 Optional Nitsche's method.

 Similar to xfem8/xfem9 but now 3D.

xfem13

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a freely floating cylinder
 (force=0,torque=0).
 eXtended FEM approach with embedded particle condition on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Prebuild eltree for all elements crossing the interface.
 Removal of elements from eltree if integration area is too small.
 High-order exact integration for small integration areas.

 Similar to xfem8+xfem9 but now with freely floating cylinder.

xfem14

 3D Stokes problem on a cubic domain with a freely floating sphere (F=0,M=0).
 eXtended FEM approach with embedded particle condition on the sphere.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Prebuild eltree for all elements crossing the interface.
 Removal of elements from eltree if integration volume is too small.
 High-order exact integration for small integration volumes.
 Optional symmetric matrix.
 Optional Nitsche's method.

 Similar to xfem13 but now 3D.

xfem15

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a freely floating cylinder
 (force=0,torque=0).
 eXtended FEM approach with embedded particle condition on the cylinder.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Prebuild eltree for all elements crossing the interface.
 Removal of elements from eltree if integration area is too small.
 High-order exact integration for small integration areas.

 Similar to xfem13, but now with an elliptical particle.

xfem16

 2D Stokes problem on a square domain with a cylindrical shaped drop
 eXtended FEM approach with weak embedded interface conditions for
 a coupling of velocities on the interface between the two fluids.
 Fluids described by layers.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Prebuild eltree for all elements crossing the interface.
 Removal of elements from eltree if integration area is too small.
 High-order exact integration for small integration areas.
 Optional different weighting for both sides of the interface.
 Optional symmetric matrix.
 Optional Nitsche's method.
 Optional Baumann-Oden method.

 Similar to xfem4 but now with embedded interface conditions

xfem17

 3D Stokes problem on a cubic domain with a spherical shaped drop
 eXtended FEM approach with weak embedded interface conditions for
 a coupling of velocities on the interface between the two fluids.
 Fluids described by layers.
 Quadtree+triangle subdivision for integration.
 Prebuild eltree for all elements crossing the interface.
 Removal of elements from eltree if integration volume is too small.
 High-order exact integration for small integration volumes.
 Optional different weighting for both sides of the interface.
 Optional symmetric matrix.
 Optional Nitsche's method.
 Optional Baumann-Oden method.

 Similar to xfem16 but now 3D.

